# Run create_table_foreign_key_with_complex with InnoDB-native foreign keys
# (innodb_native_foreign_keys=ON, set via the companion -master.opt) instead of
# MySQL 9.7's SQL-layer FK default. The body is sourced verbatim from the base
# test so both FK modes share one set of statements; only the recorded binlog
# differs (native mode handles FKs inside InnoDB, so row events carry no
# USE_SQL_FOREIGN_KEY_F flag). The matrix verifies the leak-check holds in both modes.
--source suite/villagesql/create_table/t/create_table_foreign_key_with_complex.test
